WEBVTT

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.360
I don't forgive you!  Let's duel!

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:16.680
Revolver!  If I win, I'll hold 
you responsible for everything!

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.670
If I lose, I'll give you Flame!

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.180
Fine.  I have no objections.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.330
Big trouble, Boss!

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.170
I can't hear what they're saying, but I 
think Revolver and Soulburner are gonna duel!

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:33.200
Film it!

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:33.980
Okay!

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.040
Even without sound, this is a big scoop!

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.770
You sure this is okay, Playmaker?

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.510
Leave them be.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:46.770
Until Soulburner duels Revolver, 
he can't sort out his feelings.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:50.240
They can't work together 
if they harbor ill will.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.960
If you insist.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.270
Here I go!

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.510
Duel!

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.190
My turn!

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.740
I summon Salamangreat Wolvie!

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:17.740
Then I activate the spell card, Fury of Fire!

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:23.290
I Special Summon up to two 
Salamangreats from my hand!

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:26.140
Appear, Salamangreat Parro!

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.610
Salamangreat Falco!

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.650
Link Summon!

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.820
Link 3 Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.180
I set one card and end my turn!

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:46.260
He brought out Heatleo from the start?

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.820
He's going all out.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.430
Soulburner.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:55.800
You let your emotions take control, 
challenging him to a duel, risking me irresponsibly.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:01.030
Do you understand what 
future this will lead to?

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.140
I don't care about the future.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:07.770
I'll crush him and get 
revenge for my Mom and Dad!

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.960
I know how you feel, but 
you should talk to him-

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.490
If you're worried that 
I'll lose, don't worry!

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.350
It's clear that you're not listening to me.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.960
My turn.  I draw.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.960
What will Revolver do?

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:32.060
He's not the type of duelist 
who'll go easy on a challenger.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.040
He'll take this seriously.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.250
It's your turn!  Hurry up!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.970
I end my turn.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.200
What?

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.110
What?  For real?

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:48.400
What's going on?

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.120
He didn't do anything.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.600
Is Revolver intending to lose?

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.660
I don't sense anything from his soul.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.160
What's the meaning of this, Revolver?

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.510
Didn't you hear me?  I ended my turn.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.930
Stop messing around!

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.860
My turn!  I draw!

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:14.360
I summon Salamangreat Jack Jaguar!

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.610
Soulburner's monsters have 
more ATK than Revolver's LP!

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.980
Revolver!  I don't care if 
you don't want to fight!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.210
Heatleo attacks you directly!

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.720
Revolver's LP...

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.050
The next attack will end this duel.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:14.310
Our lives aren't forever

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:21.100
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:28.420
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:34.990
Sharing hope for the future

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:41.740
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:48.970
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:55.680
I want to share your pain

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:30.290
I attack with Jack Jaguar-

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.400
I knew he couldn't attack.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.810
Soulburner...

00:05:53.160 --> 00:06:00.640
If I win like this, it 
won't look cool at all!

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:03.130
Yeah, not cool.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.670
Be quiet.

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:05.890
Okay.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.360
Satisfied?

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.580
Of course not!

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.050
I don't even know your identity!

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:16.360
And I can't duel you!

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.530
What am I supposed to do?

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.450
I'm Ryoken Kogami.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.760
The son of Kiyoshi Kogami - 
who started the Lost Incident.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:27.980
What?

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:34.290
He finally revealed his own identity!

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.500
They stopped dueling.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:40.800
What do you think Soulburner and 
Revolver are talking about, Boss?

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.490
How should I know?

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.920
Just because I know your 
identity doesn't mean-

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:54.900
Soulburner, Revolver was eight 
years old during the Lost Incident.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.860
About the same age as us.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:03.330
He reported the incident because he 
felt guilty about Dr. Kogami's actions.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:07.810
In other words, Revolver saved you.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:09.130
What?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:13.810
And the perpetrator - Dr. 
Kogami - is already dead.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:14.790
Dead?

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.730
Revolver isn't responsible 
for the Lost Incident.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:24.060
Damn!  What's going on?

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.090
Calm down, Soulburner.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.660
I know!

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:34.240
Soulburner, we'll only be working together 
until we defeat the Light Ignis.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:41.100
If we survive, we'll eventually have to 
fight each other with your Ignis on the line.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:45.420
Can you keep your anger down until then?

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:47.380
Revolver...

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:49.020
Follow me.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:51.250
There's something I want to show you.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:52.760
Show us?

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.230
What do you think, Aqua?

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.800
His heart is calm.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.600
He's not trying to trick you.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:01.400
I trust Aqua.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:05.440
Ghost Girl and Soulburner, what will you do?

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.070
I'm okay.

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:10.840
Let's hear him out.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:16.040
Fine.  But if he's tricking us, he'll pay!

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.930
Follow me.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:24.670
Let's go.

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:30.860
Everyone is going inside.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.070
What's that?

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:36.520
The gate's closing, Boss!

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:38.040
Jump in!

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.010
Where are we?

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.200
What?  Seriously?

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.420
This is...

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.190
The Tower of Hanoi!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:10.460
This is the former LINK VRAINS?

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.440
It's still around?

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:17.370
That's the Tower of Hanoi!

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:19.370
Shh!  You're too loud!

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:22.330
Why did you bring us here?

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:26.300
Don't tell me you're planning to 
bring back the Tower of Hanoi?

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:28.150
That is what I'm saying.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:31.310
Seriously?

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.070
I'm serious.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:37.600
In order to find the Light Ignis, 
I'll restart the Tower of Hanoi.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:43.040
By modding the tower's systems, 
it'll emit a powerful scan program.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:48.510
We'll be able to find the Light Ignis's 
location, no matter where it's hiding in the net.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:50.720
Is this possible?

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:55.350
This tower's systems are capable 
of emitting a powerful scan.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:02.550
But to achieve this, I need an excellent 
programmer that can use Ignis algorithms.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:07.150
I see.  That's why you needed Blood Shepherd.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:11.680
Unfortunately, Blood Shepherd was erased.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:19.460
Revolver, we all agree that 
Lightning must be defeated.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:23.540
But the Tower of Hanoi 
can be a powerful weapon.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:27.100
How do we know you won't betray us?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:31.420
You haven't forgotten what 
you did to us, have you?

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.660
You don't need to worry that I'll betray you.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.890
What's that?

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:45.360
This will be the main program that'll 
reactivate the Tower of Hanoi.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:49.140
We'll work together to build this.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:53.510
In other words, the Hanoi 
are only a part of the plan.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:57.740
You can stop this plan whenever you want.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.350
I see.

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:03.200
Fine.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:06.500
We believe in different futures.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:12.180
But by working together on this 
plan, we may find a new future.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:14.150
I'll remember that.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:15.470
No way!

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:17.890
Playmaker and Revolver are teaming up?

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:20.890
If so, this is a huge scoop!

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:22.970
We'll get a big bonus-

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:26.270
Sorry, but I can't let you leave.

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:34.410
You're staying with me for a while.

00:11:57.390 --> 00:12:00.970
What a crazy task we accepted.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:05.620
I can't believe we're the ones 
bringing back the Tower of Hanoi.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:11.240
But if this allows us to strike first 
against Lightning, it's worth doing.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:13.930
We must find Lightning, no matter what.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:15.650
You're right.

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:17.390
Just wait, Jin.

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:23.600
Takeru, let's step outside.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:29.170
You don't agree with the plan?

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:30.810
Of course not!

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.060
Team up with the Knights of Hanoi?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.870
I have one question.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:36.630
What?

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:40.380
Why did Revolver invite you?

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.870
Because he wanted to talk to me.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:48.180
Revolver was searching for 
an excellent programmer.

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.490
You're not one.

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:52.450
That's true, but...

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:58.470
Revolver only needed to invite 
Playmaker and the others.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:01.200
Even if he wanted my help...

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:06.450
...he could've discussed it with Playmaker, 
and then gradually got me involved.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.200
He doesn't need you.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.200
That's not true.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.570
I'm part of Playmaker's team!

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:15.570
No, he definitely doesn't need you.

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:22.050
Revolver knew you'll be angry with 
him, so that would be a problem.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.050
When you put it that way, you're right.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:28.980
He knew that'd happen, but 
he still invited you.  Why?

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:31.650
Well...  Why?

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:35.800
Maybe he wanted to apologize to you.

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:39.600
I end my turn.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:42.190
That's why he dueled like that?

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:48.050
Humans don't speak their true 
feelings out loud.  Or am I wrong?

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:52.660
You understand humans better than me.

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:56.250
It feels nice to hear that.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.200
Are you okay?

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:19.810
I'm fine.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:23.640
You're worried about me?

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:26.260
That's my role.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:28.600
Don't say that.

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:31.540
Haru, you're special.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:35.710
You're my one and only younger brother.

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:38.740
I'm not your real brother.

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:45.060
Lightning ordered me to pretend to be your 
brother in order to control your emotions.

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:47.050
I know.

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:50.690
But I won't forget that we were brothers.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:54.200
You carry the burden of the Ignis' future.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.750
I'm nothing more than a prototype.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.510
You're more important than me.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:04.460
Besides, I don't know what it 
really means to be brothers.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.420
Eventually, we'll become one.

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:11.070
You're right.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:15.440
Then maybe I'll understand how you feel.

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:19.800
What is it, bro?

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:21.490
You wanted to talk?

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:25.690
Yusaku is searching for Lightning.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.060
The master seems busy.

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:32.420
If they find him, we're probably 
going to have to fight.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:35.680
And I really feel something bad will happen.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:38.130
Fight, bro!

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:39.540
You don't seem worried.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.940
Don't stop me, Mother.

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:45.620
What era are you from?

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.790
Besides, that's my line!

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.240
Nice retort!

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.370
I did a joke of a joke!

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.460
And you had a retort for both!

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:54.670
Impressive, bro!

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:57.670
Don't explain jokes!

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:58.680
Enough.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:02.300
I wanted to tell you that 
I'll fulfill my promise.

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:03.270
Promise?

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:06.280
Yeah.  I'll make you smart.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:09.510
Well...  I won't do that, 
but it'll end up that way.

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.600
Are you serious, bro?

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:12.520
Yes.

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:14.450
Can I dance?

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.720
Hooray!  Hooray!

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:17.960
You're done?

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.300
I'm done!

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:21.560
This was physical comedy.

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:23.380
Stop explaining!

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:25.030
Okay, let's do this.

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:28.040
Live up to my expectations.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:43.640
It's finished.

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:46.330
If we can find Lightning's location...

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:48.620
It's finally time to fight.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:51.090
Yusaku, want me to go with you?

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:55.710
No.  There's no guarantee 
we'll survive this fight.

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:59.080
Kusanagi, don't worry.  
Because we're going too.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:05.410
We feel safer if you're 
watching over us, Kusanagi.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.270
Leave this to us, Kusanagi.

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:12.670
Fine.  Install this before you go.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.110
What's that?  I gotta eat 
something weird again?

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:19.860
It's a powered-up version of the 
program I gave you last time.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:23.310
No matter how powerful the security...

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:28.790
...it creates a backdoor from your 
location to broadcast your status.

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:31.400
So it overwrites from the inside.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:34.400
Copy this and give it to everyone.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:36.680
Then you can share information.

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:37.690
Okay.

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:39.270
I'm counting on you, everyone.

00:17:39.270 --> 00:17:40.530
Leave it to us!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:43.250
Don't worry.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.850
We promise to bring back your brother.

00:18:05.340 --> 00:18:06.890
Where's Ghost Girl?

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:09.780
I had her go to LINK VRAINS.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.600
To LINK VRAINS?

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:16.770
Just in case.  If something happens 
to LINK VRAINS, she'll deal with it.

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:20.290
And she can also talk to my brother.

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:23.980
That's a wise decision.

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:26.750
Spectre, what about your teammates?

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.420
I had them stay behind.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:33.160
Because we need backup from the outside.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:38.010
We're ready.

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:56.560
Activate scan program!

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:27.690
Prepare for impact!  Anti-glare protection!

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:30.660
Fire!

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:41.800
What's going on?

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:45.160
A powerful scan on the network!

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:46.430
What?

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:49.410
Is this the calamity you were talking about?

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:52.780
What?

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:53.910
Hey, look!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.050
It's started.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:06.240
Look!

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.660
What is that?

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:12.750
What's this?

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:16.120
It's a mirror world - a 
duplicate of LINK VRAINS.

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:20.280
It was entirely hidden by LINK VRAINS' data.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:23.350
That's why we couldn't find it.

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:27.650
That's where Lightning is!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:32.080
Hey, isn't this...

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:37.290
They've discovered the existence 
of Mirror LINK VRAINS.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:41.130
A little bit quicker than I expected.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.490
Bohman's operation hasn't been completed yet.

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:46.490
It's fine.

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:52.100
Let's strike back without 
relying on his help.

